.TH CENTURION 1 "2026-09-26" "0.1.0" "Centurion Manual"
.SH NAME
Centurion \- subtitle workflow CLI (transcribe, translate, dub, quality)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Centurion
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Centurion is a subtitle workflow CLI: transcribe audio/video (ASR or OCR),
align to a script, translate, dub, and build ASS/SRT/TXT subtitles.
All core pipelines run as a DAG; run
.B Centurion pipeline-graph \-c <command>
to preview topology.
.SH QUICK START (3 commands)
.nf
Centurion asr media.mp4
Centurion translate media.centurion.json --target zh
Centurion build media.centurion.json --format ass
.fi
Or run
.B Centurion init
for an interactive wizard that writes centurion.config.json and the recommended command chain.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output the result summary as machine-readable JSON (suppresses human lines; script-consumable).
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Preview DAG, involved models and provider unit costs without executing.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show full execution info (step timings and per-stage logs).
.TP
.B \-\-lang <CODE>
Runtime UI language (e.g. zh-CN).
.TP
.B \-\-profile <NAME>
Provider selection profile: offline / fast / quality / cheap.
.TP
.B \-\-github-proxy <URL> / \-\-no-github-proxy
GitHub download acceleration (mirror) control.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Interactive wizard: generate centurion.config.json + recommended command chain.
.TP
.B asr <INPUT_FILE>
Auto subtitle generation: audio/video -> transcription/diarization/splitting/alignment -> intermediate file.
.TP
.B ocr <INPUT_FILE>
Subtitle OCR from video frames (RapidOCR/LLM) -> splitting/cleaning -> intermediate file.
.TP
.B from-script <INPUT_FILE> <SCRIPT_FILE>
Script alignment: transcribe media against the given script and map the timeline.
.TP
.B correct <CENTURION_FILE>
Subtitle correction against reference script/audio timeline (timeline-only/text-only/both).
.TP
.B translate <CENTURION_FILE>
LLM translation with glossary and target script 1:1 alignment; bilingual support.
.TP
.B dub <CENTURION_FILE>
Media dubbing: speaker profiling -> TTS -> time alignment -> mixing -> WAV.
.TP
.B convert <INPUT_FILE>
Parse ASS/SRT/TXT subtitles into the Centurion intermediate file.
.TP
.B build <CENTURION_FILE>
Build intermediate file into ASS/SRT/TXT subtitles.
.TP
.B quality <INPUT_FILE>
Quality report (.json/.html), \-\-fix auto-repair, \-\-fail-on CI gates.
.TP
.B pipeline-graph
Render a command's DAG topology (no execution); \-c selects asr/ocr/from-script/translate/dub/correct/convert.
.TP
.B validate <files>
Validate Centurion intermediate files against the IR schema.
.TP
.B migrate <file>
Migrate intermediate files to a newer IR schema version (\-\-to).
.TP
.B update
Self-update from GitHub Releases.
.TP
.B models
Model registry management: list / install / verify / remove.
.TP
.B providers
Provider inspection: list / test (capabilities, cost, latency, quality).
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Execution failure (missing model, pipeline/IO errors).
.TP
.B 2
Usage errors (reserved; parse errors are reported by the CLI itself).
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled by user (Ctrl+C).
.SH CONFIGURATION
centurion.config.json in the current directory (or up two levels). Environment variables override it:
CENTURION_PROFILE, CENTURION_LANG, CENTURION_GITHUB_PROXY, CENTURION_LOG_LEVEL, CENTURION_JSON, CENTURION_OUTPUT_FORMAT.
CLI arguments take precedence over both.
.SH EXAMPLES
See the samples/ directory for media, subtitles, and intermediate files.
.nf
Centurion models list
Centurion providers list
Centurion convert samples/test.srt --dry-run
Centurion quality samples/sample.centurion.json --fail-on cps>20
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
GitHub Releases for the binary; issue tracker for bug reports.
